---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Editor from '../components/Editor.jsx';
const pages={
'resize-image':{title:'Resize Images Without Borders — Proportional | PlainMile',description:'Resize JPG, PNG and WebP proportionally without white borders or cropping. Set maximum pixel dimensions, or choose exact-size padding or crop.',heading:'Resize images proportionally without white borders',lead:'Keep the original aspect ratio by default. Set maximum width and height without padding or cropping, or explicitly choose an exact-size canvas.',use:'For photos, forms and upload portals requiring smaller images.',hint:'Proportional mode does not enlarge small originals, and Same as original keeps the source JPG, PNG or WebP format. Exact-size Fit may add borders; Fill and crop removes edges. Exact-size output never silently reduces pixel dimensions to meet an optional KB limit.'},
'compress-image-to-size':{title:'Compress Image to a Target KB Online | PlainMile',description:'Reduce JPG and WebP file sizes to a requested maximum KB. Verify actual bytes, with optional downscaling, in your browser.',heading:'Compress an image below a KB limit',lead:'Set a maximum file size (for example 50, 100 or 200 KB). We inspect the real exported bytes, not a predicted estimate.',use:'For application portals or online forms that reject files exceeding a specified size.',hint:'The default export is JPG for size control. If you upload a transparent PNG/WebP, JPG turns transparency white. Switch to Same as original or PNG/WebP when transparency is required; PNG is lossless and may exceed very small limits.'},
'signature-resizer':{title:'Signature Image Resizer — Pixels and KB | PlainMile',description:'Scale a signature image within pixel and KB limits without uploading it, or choose exact dimensions with padding or cropping.',heading:'Resize a scanned signature for a form',lead:'Set maximum dimensions and file-size limits. If the form requires exact pixels, choose an exact-size mode before exporting.',use:'For portals with image-size and file-size requirements.',hint:'Same as original preserves PNG transparency. A KB limit is optional and disabled until you enter one; for strict limits PNG can be too large. Only choose JPG or WebP when accepted by the receiving form.'},
'bulk-image-resizer':{title:'Bulk Image Resizer — Local ZIP Download | PlainMile',description:'Resize up to 30 JPG, PNG or WebP files proportionally without white borders in your browser and download a ZIP.',heading:'Resize multiple images together',lead:'Set maximum dimensions and download a ZIP. Each image keeps its original aspect ratio, with individual output dimensions available for review.',use:'For consistent image collections, catalogs and repeated uploads.',hint:'Each item keeps its original JPG, PNG or WebP format by default. Even a one-image batch downloads a ZIP. Exact-size modes can add borders or crop edges.'},
'passport-photo-print':{title:'4×6 Passport Photo Print Sheet — Free | PlainMile',description:'Repeat one manually cropped 2×2-inch photo six times on a 4×6-inch JPEG print sheet locally. No upload.',heading:'Create a 4×6 photo print sheet',lead:'Frame an existing photo and generate a 1200×1800 JPEG with six 600×600 photo tiles for printing at 300 pixels per inch.',use:'For printing six square copies where 2×2-inch size is specifically required.',hint:'This is only a print layout, not a passport approval or automatic compliance check. Many authorities prohibit digitally altered photos; verify official instructions.'}
};
export function getStaticPaths(){return ['resize-image','compress-image-to-size','signature-resizer','bulk-image-resizer','passport-photo-print'].map(tool=>({params:{tool}}));}
const tool=Astro.params.tool;const page=pages[tool];
const examples={
  'resize-image':'Example: A 1920 × 1080 photograph limited to 800 × 800 pixels becomes 800 × 450 without borders. To output exactly 800 × 800, switch to a fixed-size padded or cropped mode.',
  'compress-image-to-size':'Example: For a 100 KB upload limit, keep the maximum size at 100 and start with JPG quality at 90%. The final downloaded bytes are checked; if the goal is unreachable, lower quality or allow a smaller image.',
  'signature-resizer':'Example: If a form requests exactly 300 × 100 pixels, select a fixed-size mode. Proportional mode uses those numbers as maximums and may produce a smaller canvas.',
  'bulk-image-resizer':'Example: A 1600 × 900 JPG and an 800 × 1200 PNG with 800 × 800 maximums become 800 × 450 JPG and 533 × 800 PNG inside the same ZIP.',
  'passport-photo-print':'Example: The tool produces a 1200 × 1800 JPEG with six 600 × 600 copies, tagged 300 DPI. At print time, select 4 × 6 inches and 100% scaling.'
};
const guide={"resize-image":{"heading":"Proportional, padded or cropped resizing?","intro":"The default proportional mode fits your image within the maximum width and height while preserving its shape. It does not add borders, crop the image or enlarge small originals. To make an exact 600 × 400 pixel file, choose Crop edges to fit (part of the image may be cut off) or Keep whole image, add space (which may leave empty borders).","q":[["Why does the output differ from the maximum dimensions?","Proportional resizing preserves the original aspect ratio and fits inside both maximum dimensions. The expected output appears before processing."],["How do I get exactly the dimensions I enter?","Choose an exact-size mode. Fit preserves the image but may add borders; Fill and crop makes an exact canvas by trimming the edges."],["Will enlarging a small image improve its detail?","No. More pixels cannot restore detail absent from a low-resolution source. Default proportional resizing intentionally avoids upscaling."],["Why did linked width and height become smaller?","If you enable Sync width and height in an exact-size mode, oversized dimensions are reduced together to keep the original proportions within the browser’s 10,000-pixel edge and 32-megapixel output limits."]],"links":[["/compress-image-to-size/","Compress under a KB limit"],["/bulk-image-resizer/","Resize a batch"]]},"compress-image-to-size":{"heading":"Use the size limit from your upload form","intro":"Enter the maximum permitted KB, such as 50 or 100. The editor checks the actual output bytes after encoding. JPEG and WebP can reduce file size by lowering quality. When the limit is too small for the selected dimensions, allowing smaller dimensions may help.","q":[["How do I make a photo smaller than 100 KB?","Enter 100 for the maximum size and choose JPEG or WebP when accepted. The output must also meet any minimum pixel dimensions set by the destination."],["Why can PNG be difficult to compress?","PNG is lossless and its quality slider has no effect. Detailed photos often remain larger; select JPEG or WebP only if the destination supports the format and transparency is not lost unexpectedly."]],"links":[["/resize-image/","Resize a single photo"],["/signature-resizer/","Resize a signature"]]},"signature-resizer":{"heading":"Match pixel dimensions and the KB limit","intro":"Application forms sometimes require an exact width, height and maximum file size. Default proportional mode stays inside maximum dimensions without padding; choose fixed-size Fit or Fill and crop if the form requires exact output pixels. The tool does not remove a scanned background or validate a signature.","q":[["Should I export a transparent signature?","Same as original keeps the source PNG or WebP format and existing transparency. If you choose JPEG, transparency is replaced by white. Follow the receiving form’s format requirement."],["Can this tool guarantee the form accepts my signature?","No. File format, minimum image quality and signature validity depend on the receiving organization."]],"links":[["/compress-image-to-size/","Compress to a file-size limit"],["/resize-image/","Resize a photo"]]},"bulk-image-resizer":{"heading":"Apply one resize rule to a set of pictures","intro":"Choose up to 30 JPEG, PNG or WebP files, 160 MB total. By default, each picture fits within the maximum width and height, retains its input format and is not upscaled, cropped or padded. Exact-size Fit and Fill and crop remain optional. One or more results are packaged into a ZIP.","q":[["What if my photos have different aspect ratios?","The default Fit within mode preserves each photo's aspect ratio with no added border. Fit adds padding to an exact canvas, while Fill and crop trims the edges."],["Are originals overwritten?","No. A ZIP containing new output files is downloaded. Your original images are not modified."]],"links":[["/resize-image/","Resize a single image"],["/compress-image-to-size/","Compress to KB"]]},"passport-photo-print":{"heading":"Print size and official photo requirements","intro":"This tool places six identical 600 × 600 pixel tiles on a 1200 × 1800 pixel JPEG and sets its density to 300 DPI. Print on 4 × 6 inch paper at actual size; some print dialogs automatically zoom, add margins or crop borderless prints.","q":[["Does this verify a passport or visa photo?","No. It does not check lighting, pose, background, clothing or official acceptance. Follow the issuing authority’s instructions; digital alterations may not be allowed."],["Why does the printed photo measure incorrectly?","Confirm 4 × 6 inch paper, 100% scale and any borderless-cropping option in your printer or lab settings."]],"links":[["/resize-image/","Resize a digital photo"],["/compress-image-to-size/","Compress a photo"]]}}[tool];
---
<Base path={'/'+tool+'/'} title={page.title} description={page.description}>
<section class="page-head"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Image tools</a> / {page.heading}</p><h1>{page.heading}</h1><p class="lead">{page.lead}</p></section>
<Editor client:load lang="en" tool={tool}/>
{tool!=='passport-photo-print'&&<p class="editor-disclosure">Tip: You can paste a screenshot with Ctrl+V (or ⌘V on Mac) before choosing your image. Use the controls above to prepare the output.</p>}
<section class="reference" aria-label="Help for this tool">
<h2>{guide.heading}</h2><p>{guide.intro}</p><p>{examples[tool]}</p><p>{page.use}</p><p>{page.hint}</p>
<h2>Common questions</h2>
{guide.q.map(([question,answer])=><div class="qa"><h3>{question}</h3><p>{answer}</p></div>)}
<h2>Related tools</h2><ul class="related-links">{guide.links.map(([href,label])=><li><a href={href}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul>
<p class="editor-disclosure">Images are processed in this browser tab. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</section>
</Base>
